<title>USA: Yellow expands to Australia, New Zealand.</title>
<headline>Yellow expands to Australia, New Zealand.</headline>
<dateline>OVERLAND PARK, Kan. 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yellow Freight System, a unit of Yellow Corp, said Tuesday it has begun offering less-than-containerload service to and from Australia.</p>
<p>In November, such service will expand into New Zealand and the Philippines.</p>
<p>Shipments to and from North America will use the Port of Long Beach and three strategic partners -- Intramar in Australia, New Zealand Express in New Zealand and Business Logistics Inc in the Philippines.</p>
<p>Service to Vietnam, Malaysia, India and the United Arab Emirates will be added later this year and in early 1997.</p>
<p>	   -- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787</p>
